@startuml
title MCPVault domain boundaries (conceptual, not storage ownership)
hide empty methods
class Note {
  path
  lifecycle
  task_status
  epistemic_status
}
class Revision {
  repositoryId
  path
  sha256
}
class Claim {
  normalizedId
  text
  status
}
class EvidenceLocator {
  revision
  heading
  blockId
  startLine
  endLine
  quoteHash
}
class RelationOccurrence {
  id
  source
  relation
  direction
  targetReference
  target
  syntax
  locator
  kind
  extraction
  evidenceState
}
class MOCMembership {
  mocPath
  memberPath
  inputRevision
}
class SynthesisBasis {
  question
  inputs
  explanations
  choices
  counterexamples
  unresolvedQuestions
}
enum RelationKind {
  supports
  contradicts
  supersedes
  derived_from
  depends_on
  implements
  blocked_by
  answers_questions
  tests
  related
  same_as
  close_match
  version_of
  refines
}
RelationOccurrence --> RelationKind : typed relation or extracted link
Note "1" -- "1..*" Revision : observed versions
Revision "1" -- "0..*" Claim : scoped IDs, not global keys
RelationOccurrence "0..*" --> "1" Revision : source
RelationOccurrence "0..*" --> "0..1" Revision : resolved target
RelationOccurrence "0..*" --> "0..1" Claim : source claim
Claim "0..*" --> "0..*" EvidenceLocator : authored evidence
MOCMembership "0..*" --> "1" Note : member
MOCMembership "0..*" --> "1" Note : MOC
SynthesisBasis "0..*" --> "2..8" Revision : exact input pins
note bottom of MOCMembership
  Membership is topic composition, not subclass inheritance.
  Parent navigation and saved input coverage are separate.
end note
note bottom of RelationOccurrence
  Repeated same-pair occurrences remain distinct.
  Authored / extracted / inferred are not truth scores.
  stable_id is not an unchecked global identity.
  No association implies deletion or grants access.
end note
@enduml
